cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroLIF-SKY130 in research or academic work, please cite this repository."
title: "NeuroLIF-SKY130: Transistor-Level Leaky Integrate-and-Fire Neuron with Weighted Synaptic Input and Robustness Characterization"
type: software

authors:
  - name: "preetopritam"

repository-code: "https://github.com/preetopritam/NeuroLIF-SKY130"

license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-31"

keywords:
  - neuromorphic computing
  - leaky integrate-and-fire neuron
  - LIF neuron
  - SKY130
  - CMOS
  - weighted synapse
  - analog VLSI
  - physical design
  - KLayout
  - ngspice

abstract: >
  NeuroLIF-SKY130 is a pre-silicon educational neuromorphic circuit-design
  project implementing a transistor-level leaky integrate-and-fire neuron
  using the open SKY130 PDK. The design includes a corrected 2-bit weighted
  electronic synapse, membrane integration and leak, a CMOS Schmitt threshold
  detector, output buffering and spike-controlled reset. The public repository
  includes transistor-level validation, PVT and deterministic variation
  summaries, physical-layout construction scripts and DRC, connectivity and
  LVS verification evidence.